###############################################################################
# ADMIN — auction oversight (Dev 4)
# The whole file can be run top to bottom (request 1 passes its id to the requests after it)
#
# Covered so far: ADM-001 an admin can cancel an inappropriate auction
# with the action and reason recorded
#
# 💡 How this differs from AUC-006:
#    a seller can only cancel DRAFT / SCHEDULED, and only their own
#    an admin can also cancel ACTIVE — that is why this requirement exists
#    (an inappropriate auction that is running shouldn't have to wait until it ends)
#
# 💡 It cannot be cancelled once ended (SOLD / UNSOLD) — a sold auction has a winner,
#    a price and an order behind it; undoing it is a refund, not a cancellation
#
# ⚠️ Every cancellation writes admin_actions in the same transaction (ADM-004)
#    if the cancellation fails, no audit row is left behind
###############################################################################

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@sellerA = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@buyer   = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@catCollectibles = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000103

# AUTH-008 — paste the tokens from `pnpm --filter api exec prisma db seed`
@adminToken   =
@sellerAToken =
@buyerToken   =

#=============================================================================
# 1. The oversight list (ADM-001)
#=============================================================================

### sees auctions in every status, including unpublished DRAFTs. expect 200
# Auctions get reported before publishing as much as after, so admins need to see drafts too
# Newest first — oversight follows whatever just appeared
# ⚠️ reservePrice must not appear at all, even for an admin (SRS section 6)
#    deciding an auction is inappropriate never needs the seller's acceptable price
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### filter by status. expect 200 + every item is ACTIVE
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions?status=ACTIVE&limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### a status that doesn't exist. expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions?status=NONSENSE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### a regular user can't access it. expect 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### not logged in. expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions

#=============================================================================
# 2. Prepare a running auction to cancel
#=============================================================================

### create a draft that has already started
# @name liveDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Admin cancel test item",
  "description": "Already started, bids coming in",
  "categoryId": "{{catCollectibles}}",
  "condition": "USED",
  "startingPrice": 3000,
  "minBidIncrement": 100,
  "reservePrice": 4500,
  "scheduledStartAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "scheduledEndAt": "2026-12-31T00:00:00.000Z",
  "imageUrls": ["https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Admin"]
}

@liveId = {{liveDraft.response.body.$.id}}

### publish. expect 200 + status ACTIVE
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/drafts/{{liveId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### a buyer bids (so someone has to be notified on cancellation). expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/bids
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 3000, "clientRequestId": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333301" }

### the seller tries to cancel it themselves. expect 400
# AUC-006 forbids sellers from cancelling an ACTIVE auction — people are bidding on what they see
POST {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Withdrawing it myself" }

#=============================================================================
# 3. Cancellation by an admin (ADM-001)
#=============================================================================

### empty reason. expect 400
# ADM-001 requires a reason — unlike AUC-006, where the seller may leave it blank
# A seller withdrawing their own item owes nobody an explanation, but an admin overturning someone else's must be answerable
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "   " }

### a regular user can't cancel, however good the reason. expect 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Obviously counterfeit" }

### the auction's own seller can't use the admin route either. expect 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "It's my own item" }

### an admin actually cancels. expect 200 + status CANCELLED
# PATCH, not DELETE, because the auction is not deleted — it stays readable as CANCELLED
# with the reason, which is what makes it auditable afterwards
#
# Within one single transaction:
#   1. auctions.status = CANCELLED + cancellationReason + endedAt
#   2. a new auction_events row CANCELLED (actorUserId = admin)
#   3. a new admin_actions row CANCEL_AUCTION + note (ADM-004)
#   4. AUCTION_CANCELLED notifications for the seller + bidders + watchers (NOT-004)
# and only after commit is `auction:cancelled` broadcast to the room
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Copyright-infringing item" }

### cancelling again. expect 400
# and there must be no extra admin_actions row from the failed attempt
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/{{liveId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Cancelling once more" }

### an id that doesn't exist. expect 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000009ff/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Does not exist" }

### an id that is not a UUID. expect 400 from ParseUUIDPipe
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/auctions/not-a-uuid/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Wrong format" }

#=============================================================================
# 4. Verify results after cancelling
#=============================================================================

### can the auction be read? expect 404
# CANCELLED is not in PUBLIC_AUCTION_STATUSES — it disappears from public view
GET {{baseUrl}}/auctions/{{liveId}}

### the seller is notified with the reason. expect 200
# Unlike when the seller cancels themselves (no notification) — this time it wasn't their decision
# so they are the person who most deserves an explanation
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?types=AUCTION_CANCELLED
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerAToken}}

### bidders are notified too. expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?types=AUCTION_CANCELLED
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### the admin who cancelled it isn't notified. expect 200 + meta.total 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?types=AUCTION_CANCELLED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### audit log (ADM-004 — Dev 5's). expect 200
# Must show a CANCEL_AUCTION row with note = the reason entered
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/actions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

#=============================================================================
# 5. A case that can't be cancelled — an auction that has already ended
#=============================================================================
#
# Create an auction, bid up to the reserve, let it expire, then GET /auctions/:id
# once so AUC-007 read repair closes it:
#
#   docker exec docker-postgres-1 psql -U bidnest -d bidnest_db -c \
#     "update auctions set current_end_at = now() - interval '1 second' \
#      where id = '<id>';"
#
# then try cancelling → expect 400
# A sold auction has a winner and a price behind it; undoing it is a refund,
# which is a different matter from cancelling, and no V1 requirement covers it yet
#=============================================================================

### WebSocket: the auction room gets `auction:cancelled` as soon as the cancellation succeeds
#
#   const socket = io('http://localhost:4000/auctions', {
#     transports: ['websocket']
#   });
#   socket.emit('auction:join', { auctionId: '<liveId>' });
#   socket.on('auction:cancelled', (e) => console.log(e.status, e.reason));
#
# the payload has auctionId / status / endedAt / reason
# ⚠️ It says nothing about which admin cancelled it — "shut down by an admin" is a matter
#    between the system and the seller, not something the auction room needs to know
#
# 💡 The same event also fires when the seller cancels themselves (AUC-006) — one event
#    must always mean the same thing, no matter who triggered it
